SMALL → BIG
   ↓
WIDENING
   ↓
AUTOMATIC

BIG → SMALL
   ↓
NARROWING
   ↓
EXPLICIT CAST

CHILD → PARENT
   ↓
UPCASTING

PARENT → CHILD
   ↓
DOWNCASTING
   ↓
May cause ClassCastException

Golden sentence:

> Type casting in Java is the conversion of a value or reference from one compatible type to another; primitive widening is generally automatic, primitive narrowing requires explicit casting, and reference downcasting can fail at runtime.
